  "last_updated": "2026-05-04",
  "summary": "Fishing tackle and lure brands with strong resale economics. Vintage wooden lures (Heddon, Creek Chub, Paw Paw) command premium from a dedicated collector base — original box doubles value. Modern premium (Rapala, Bagley) retains value when in unfished condition. Pacific NW salmon/steelhead specialty gear (Les Davis, Beau Mac, Luhr-Jensen) has its own niche market that's strong on eBay regardless of national trends.",
  "field_workflow": [
    "Identify maker via stamping on lure body (most are stamped on belly or lip)",
    "Photograph hooks, hardware, and box if present — original tag/box doubles value",
    "Glass-eye lures pre-1955 are premium over plastic-eye (most makers transitioned ~1955)",
    "Single hook vs double vs treble matters — original hooks add value",
    "Hairline cracks in wooden lures are tolerated; missing paint or repaints kill value",
    "For modern Rapala/Storm: discontinued colors trade at 5-10x common colors"
  ],
  "skip_list": [
    "Generic / unbranded plastic lures",
    "Made in China lures (modern aftermarket)",
    "Walmart house brand tackle",
    "Berkley Power Bait (consumable, low resale)",
    "Plano tackle boxes (mass market)",
    "Eagle Claw mass-market hooks",
    "Repainted vintage lures (any maker)",
    "Reproduction lures",
    "Lures missing original hooks (most cases)"
  ],
